Project libraries use lib/<name>/src for PlatformIO discovery and future
on-device imports. ControllerCore has portable behavior; ControllerSupport has
shared Arduino utilities. AcController, TemperatureSensor, ControllerNetwork,
ControllerWeb, and LotusLamp own the corresponding subsystem implementations.

Libraries must not reference application globals. The app composes long-lived
owners in src/controller_app.cpp. PlatformIO compiles library sources; do not
also register them in src/CMakeLists.txt. Preserve portable headers without
Arduino/FreeRTOS dependencies where possible. See README.md#firmware-components
for the source map and README.md#async-http-ownership for task ownership.
